 records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.cor-negative-mobius-overshoot"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.cor-negative-mobius-overshoot"],"id":"long.cor-negative-mobius-overshoot","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Corollary 6.29 (Negative-Möbius Boolean support overshoots $`1/2`$)","locator":"Long record Corollary 6.29, p. 52, label cor:negative-mobius-overshoot","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $N=\\{d\\ge2:\\mu(d)=-1\\}$. Isolating the $d=1$ term in Theorem 6.28 gives\n$$\nX_N(2)=\\frac12+\n       \\sum_{\\substack{d\\ge2\\\\\\mu(d)=1}}\\frac1{2^d-1}\n       \\ge\\frac12+\\frac1{63}>\\frac12,\n$$\nsince $\\mu(6)=1$. This rules out the particular candidate $N$. It does not rule out other infinite supports representing $1/2$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.cor-negative-mobius-overshoot","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.cor-negative-mobius-overshoot","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.cor-negative-mobius-overshoot%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.MobiusSignSupportNoGo.half_lt_tsum_negativeMobius%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.cor-negative-mobius-overshoot%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.MobiusSignSupportNoGo.half_lt_tsum_negativeMobius%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.MobiusSignSupportNoGo.half_lt_tsum_negativeMobius"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.cor-negative-mo